infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Unit test vs e2e test: speed vs wiring coverage
  desc Same route, two test shapes — e2e trades milliseconds for the integration seams a mock hides
  compares
    - label Unit test — one class wrapped in fakes
      children
        - label Scope: a single provider in isolation
          desc Instantiates UsersService; the repository, pipe, and guard are all mocked
        - label Speed ~2 ms per test
          desc No app boot, no HTTP, no DB — pure in-memory
        - label Pipe / guard / DB mocked away
          desc The real ValidationPipe, JwtAuthGuard, and repository never run
        - label Misses wiring bugs
          desc Cannot see a rejected field, a blocking guard, or a unique-constraint violation
    - label E2E test — whole AppModule over HTTP
      children
        - label Scope: the full assembled application
          desc compile() + createNestApplication() + app.init(), driven by supertest
        - label Speed ~hundreds of ms per test
          desc Boots the runtime and hits a real test DB on every request
        - label Real pipe / guard / DB all run
          desc Supertest sends a real request through the assembled pipeline
        - label Catches wiring bugs
          desc The pipe, guard, and real schema constraints actually fire
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
